# Audit: x86_emit_diag port to aarch64_emit_diag

Logline: Line-by-line diff of the AArch64 Tier 0 fix #1, with x86-specific-assumption review, aarch64-specific-opportunity scan, public-surface comparison, coverage-gap report, and KEEP/FIX/EXTEND recommendations.

Setup: x86_emit_diag.oo (149 lines, source of truth) and aarch64_emit_diag.oo (161 lines, port) read; x86_emit.oo:43 (import) and aarch64_emit.oo:18, 129-137 (wiring) read; oodac/ grep run for x86_diag_/aarch64_diag_/x86_emit_diag_test callers. Static analysis only. No .oo file was modified.

Beats:
  1. Side-by-side row-by-row diff with match/diff and reason.
  2. x86-specific assumptions the port may have inherited.
  3. aarch64-specific opportunities the port missed.
  4. Public surface diff table.
  5. Coverage gaps: errors caught in x86 but not aarch64.
  6. KEEP-AS-IS / FIX-IN-PORT / EXTEND-PORT recommendations.

residual: x86_emit_diag_test was never written; the x86 smoke test (x86_diag_smoke.oo) only greps for `pub fn` presence, so a runtime coverage gap is invisible to today's tests.

File: openOODA/audit/aarch64-diag-port.oot
Static analysis only. No oodac/*.oo file was modified.

---

## 1. Side-by-side comparison

All rows are 1-indexed and refer to the same source-line position in each file unless the row says "aarch64-only".

